{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QAnalysisUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QAnalysisUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QAnalysis"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QDilogarithm.eval_unique_of_pentagon_rigid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QDilogarithm.eval_unique_of_pentagon_rigid","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniqueness.lean#L97-L133","doc":"**Uniqueness of the q-dilogarithm evaluation, conditional on\npentagon rigidity.**\n\nThe conclusion is about `Li2_eval`, **not** `Li2`, and that is a\ncorrection rather than a weakening: `Li2` is not mentioned by the\n`pentagon` field, so no hypothesis about the pentagon can reach it.\nThe refuted axioms concluded `Li2.1 = Li2.1`, which the pentagon\nnever constrained.\n\nThe pentagon relation is additive in `Li2_eval`, so the difference\nof two solutions is again a solution; `pentagon_rigid` -- the\nnarrative proof's one-dimensionality step -- then forces it to\nvanish. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-dilogarithm-unique","label":"prop:q-dilogarithm-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-dilogarithm-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.unique_of_prim_rigid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.unique_of_prim_rigid","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniqueness.lean#L77-L95","doc":"**Uniqueness of the q-logarithm primitive, conditional on primitive\nrigidity.**\n\n`prim_rigid` is the narrative proof's own step: a primitive with\nvanishing counit is zero. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-logarithm-unique","label":"prop:q-logarithm-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QExponential.unique_of_flow_rigid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QExponential.unique_of_flow_rigid","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniqueness.lean#L58-L75","doc":"**Uniqueness of the q-exponential grouplike, conditional on flow\nrigidity.**\n\n`flow_rigid` is the narrative proof's own step: an element fixed by\nthe Jackson derivative with vanishing counit is zero.  Given it, the\ndifference of two grouplikes sharing `counit` and `D_q` is such an\nelement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-exponential-unique","label":"prop:q-exponential-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}